// Brings the main menu up over the game and shoots it 250 ms into its fade-in on retail
// (about a second in on ours: the waits in the one command line count milliseconds on
// retail and frames, about 4 ms each, on ours), then pops it and shoots the game three
// times, about 0.3 s, 0.45 s and 1.45 s after the pop. Retail fades the popped menu out
// over its 0.5 s with the game running under it, so the first two shots must show the
// menu going and the third must not. The waits after the pop are the level script's:
// the menu pauses the game, so they run only once it is off the stack, the same on both
// games (the first also covers the 50 ms or so before the client pauses the game).
//   .claude\skills\retail-capture\scripts\capture.ps1 -Probe probe-mfade -Map zoo -MaskNotify
probe:
waitforplayer
wait 2
stuffcmd "pushmenu main; wait 250; screenshot; wait 1500; popmenu"
wait 0.35
stuffcmd "screenshot"
wait 0.15
stuffcmd "screenshot"
wait 1
stuffcmd "screenshot"
wait 1
stuffcmd "quit"
end
